{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfkfjucU2uTogXQSXxnzP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written the candidate for refinement slot 4 and it passes the self-check (`OK`, smoke-fit ELPD-LOO −3556.8). That number comes from a 100-draw, single-chain smoke fit, so it isn't a fair comparison with the incumbent's −3568.2.\n\n**Model name:** `short_sequence_pseudoflip_dilution`\n\n**What I refined:** the incumbent, `heavy_tailed_signed_sensitivity_motif`. Its whole mechanism is kept: the second-order picture of a fair coin, the three suspected regular generators (switch-biased coin, heads-favoured trick coin, repeating motif), heavy-tailed signed sensitivity per person, and the side habit.\n\n**The single change:** how evidence is scaled by sequence length. The incumbent divides the evidence by a power of length, `(n/5)^-gamma`, which makes the evidence for 2- and 3-flip pairs grow without limit as sequences get shorter. In the new model people treat a short sequence as if it came with a few imagined, unremarkable extra flips: `((n + c)/(5 + c))^-gamma`, with `c > 0` fitted. When `c` goes to 0 this is the incumbent again. The aim is the critique's finding that in pairs of length 2–3 people choose the more-switching sequence less often than the incumbent predicts (0.744 observed vs 0.776 predicted).\n\n**Caveats:**\n- **Convergence wasn't verified.** One chain can't report R-hat, and admission's full fit still has to meet the convergence limits. A possible risk is that the new `c` and the existing `gamma` trade off against each other.\n- **PSIS-LOO was flagged unreliable** on the smoke fit: 7% of trials had Pareto k above 0.5, against a 1% tolerance. Admission's full fit will give the real verdict.\n- **Novelty wasn't checked.** The novelty pool uses only lengths 4–8, so this model differs from the incumbent there only through the fitted change in length scaling. It may come out close to the novelty threshold.\n\nThe three files (`hypothesis.md`, `model_name.txt`, `candidate.py`) are in `experiment3/model_loop/iter_2/candidate_4/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2372,"cache_read_input_tokens":92502,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2372,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6d75802-60c9-4afb-b015-cdf064e2bccf","uuid":"f162512e-6c4d-4574-a616-e20cf2b432c1","timestamp":"2026-10-06T08:29:09.052Z","request_id":"req_011CfkfjtL5LwR4RdJmVyE6h"}
